\f1\b\fs20 \cf2 Authorization for a Bilateral Release/Disclosure of Organizational and Protected Health Information\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl259\slmult1\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf2 The purpose of this release of information, which is compliant with both HIPAA and 42 CFR Part 2, is to facilitate coordinated and comprehensive healthcare while respecting client privacy and confidentiality. By adhering to HIPAA regulations, the release of information ensures that protected health information (PHI) is shared only with client consent or when permitted or required by law. It establishes the client's control over their health information and safeguards their privacy rights. Additionally, compliance with 42 CFR Part 2 ensures the confidentiality of substance use disorder (SUD) treatment information. The release of information allows for the authorized sharing of SUD-related data with healthcare providers, including treatment facilities, psychiatrists, and general care doctors, as well as lawyers and family members. This collaborative approach promotes effective care coordination, enabling the involved parties to work together in supporting the client's overall well-being while upholding the necessary legal and ethical safeguards surrounding sensitive health information.\
